</ol>

<h2>Local Weather Considerations in Temple and Bell County</h2>
<p>Metal's strengths line up well with the weather here. Spring storms between roughly March and June bring hail and strong straight-line winds, and properly fastened panels with secured trim resist wind uplift better than many other coverings. Heavy downpours run off metal quickly, which puts more emphasis on correctly sized <a href="/services/gutters-roof-drainage-temple-tx/">gutters and drainage</a> at the eaves. Wide daily temperature swings cause panels to expand and contract, so clip systems and fastener placement matter. Occasional winter freezes can also let snow and ice slide off metal suddenly, which is worth considering above walkways and entries.</p>
<p>Homes near Lake Belton or Stillhouse Hollow Lake, and older houses near downtown Temple with complex rooflines, each bring their own details. We will point out the specifics on your property during the inspection.</p>

<h2>When to Schedule a Metal Roof Inspection</h2>
<ul>
